From: Carlinkit Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] select: restore legacy closed-fd behavior for Carlinkit

Carlinkit's proprietary multithreaded daemons close and replace descriptors
while another thread is blocked in select(). Upstream commit 68514dacf271
(stable backport 145407e54fd1) made a concurrently closed descriptor visible
as ready by adding EPOLLNVAL to the select result masks. On this appliance
that wakes the old socket path during the Bluetooth-to-Wi-Fi handover and
causes intermittent CarPlay connection failure.

The proprietary userspace requires the earlier result-mask behavior. Keep the
modern select implementation, but ignore EPOLLNVAL as pre-5.15.18 did.

--- a/fs/select.c
+++ b/fs/select.c
@@ -466,11 +466,9 @@ get_max:
 }
 
-#define POLLIN_SET (EPOLLRDNORM | EPOLLRDBAND | EPOLLIN | EPOLLHUP | EPOLLERR |\
-			EPOLLNVAL)
-#define POLLOUT_SET (EPOLLWRBAND | EPOLLWRNORM | EPOLLOUT | EPOLLERR |\
-			 EPOLLNVAL)
-#define POLLEX_SET (EPOLLPRI | EPOLLNVAL)
+#define POLLIN_SET (EPOLLRDNORM | EPOLLRDBAND | EPOLLIN | EPOLLHUP | EPOLLERR)
+#define POLLOUT_SET (EPOLLWRBAND | EPOLLWRNORM | EPOLLOUT | EPOLLERR)
+#define POLLEX_SET (EPOLLPRI)
 
 static inline __poll_t select_poll_one(int fd, poll_table *wait, unsigned long in,
